{
  "releases": {
    "v1": {
      "name": "Shared lens catalog, release 1",
      "description": "The first lens catalog release: declarative forms of the four passive lens prototypes from ontola/atomic-plugins#271 and #365. Each is a subset of its code lens; its limits say what it leaves out. Declared, not verified: no host loads this catalog yet.",
      "lenses": [
        "clockify-time-entry-v1",
        "todoist-task-issue-v1",
        "raindrop-bookmark-v1",
        "solid-bookmark-v1"
      ]
    }
  },
  "lenses": {
    "clockify-time-entry-v1": {
      "name": "Clockify time entry ↔ Time entry",
      "description": "A completed Clockify time entry, as syncables reads it through the Clockify overlays, and the shared time-entry-v1 class: description, start, end and billable.",
      "source": {
        "record": {
          "provider": "clockify.me",
          "resource": "timeEntry",
          "openapi": "APIs/clockify.me/1.0.0-readonly"
        }
      },
      "target": { "class": "time-entry-v1" },
      "mapping": {
        "version": 2,
        "fields": [
          {
            "source": "/description",
            "target": "https://atomicdata.dev/properties/name"
          },
          {
            "source": "/timeInterval/start",
            "target": "work-start",
            "convert": "iso-seconds-to-ms"
          },
          {
            "source": "/timeInterval/end",
            "target": "work-end",
            "convert": "iso-seconds-to-ms"
          },
          { "source": "/billable", "target": "work-billable" }
        ]
      },
      "limits": [
        "No domain guard: the code lens refuses running timers, locked entries, non-REGULAR entries (breaks, time off) and intervals that end before they start; this mapping maps any record it is given.",
        "The description is copied as is: the code lens trims it and shows an empty one as \"Time entry\", and writes \"Time entry\" back as an empty description.",
        "projectId is not mapped: work-project links to a work-project-v1 row, which needs an identity map from provider ids to rows, not a value converter. The code lens also drops taskId when the project changes.",
        "A changed start or end must be whole seconds (Clockify's precision); the code lens additionally checks the provider's locked, custom-field and project restrictions before a write.",
        "A missing description, start or end in the table leaves the provider value unchanged; removal is not expressible.",
        "Moving the start or end leaves timeInterval.duration as it was; the provider recomputes it, and the code lens does not update it either."
      ],
      "implementation": "integrations/timesheets/devonian/clockify/lens/algebra.ts",
      "examples": [
        {
          "source": {
            "id": "entry-1",
            "description": "Write the report",
            "billable": true,
            "projectId": "project-1",
            "taskId": "task-1",
            "tagIds": ["tag-1"],
            "type": "REGULAR",
            "timeInterval": {
              "start": "2026-10-05T09:00:00Z",
              "end": "2026-10-05T10:30:00Z",
              "duration": "PT1H30M"
            }
          },
          "target": {
            "https://atomicdata.dev/properties/name": "Write the report",
            "work-start": 1791190800000,
            "work-end": 1791196200000,
            "work-billable": true
          },
          "edits": [
            {
              "target": {
                "https://atomicdata.dev/properties/name": "Write the report",
                "work-start": 1791190800000,
                "work-end": 1791198000000,
                "work-billable": false
              },
              "source": {
                "id": "entry-1",
                "description": "Write the report",
                "billable": false,
                "projectId": "project-1",
                "taskId": "task-1",
                "tagIds": ["tag-1"],
                "type": "REGULAR",
                "timeInterval": {
                  "start": "2026-10-05T09:00:00Z",
                  "end": "2026-10-05T11:00:00Z",
                  "duration": "PT1H30M"
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "target": { "work-end": 1791198000500 },
              "error": "precision"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "todoist-task-issue-v1": {
      "name": "Todoist task ↔ Issue",
      "description": "An active Todoist task (API v1), as syncables reads it through the Todoist overlays, and the shared issue-v1 class. Name and body are writable; completion and the due day are read-only.",
      "source": {
        "record": {
          "provider": "todoist.com",
          "resource": "task",
          "openapi": "APIs/todoist.com/1"
        }
      },
      "target": { "class": "issue-v1" },
      "mapping": {
        "version": 2,
        "fields": [
          {
            "source": "/content",
            "target": "https://atomicdata.dev/properties/name"
          },
          {
            "source": "/description",
            "target": "https://atomicdata.dev/task/v1/body"
          },
          {
            "source": "/checked",
            "target": "https://atomicdata.dev/task/v1/status",
            "convert": "map",
            "args": {
              "pairs": [
                [false, ["https://atomicdata.dev/task/v1/todo"]],
                [true, ["https://atomicdata.dev/task/v1/done"]]
              ]
            },
            "readOnly": true
          },
          {
            "source": "/due/date",
            "target": "https://atomicdata.dev/task/v1/due-date",
            "convert": "day-of",
            "readOnly": true
          }
        ]
      },
      "limits": [
        "No domain guard: the code lens refuses deleted tasks, an empty content and a non-boolean checked; this mapping maps any record it is given.",
        "A task without a due date has no due-date here; the code lens also removes a stale due-date from the row, which a v2 mapping cannot express.",
        "Doing and Blocked have no Todoist equivalent: a row with either status cannot be read back through this lens (unmapped-value).",
        "Assignee, labels, priority and parent are not mapped.",
        "A due date with a fixed time zone (a date-time ending in Z or an offset) is refused with bad-value: its day depends on the time zone, which day-of does not apply. The code lens takes its UTC day instead."
      ],
      "implementation": "integrations/issue-tracker/devonian/todoist/lens/index.ts",
      "examples": [
        {
          "source": {
            "id": "task-a",
            "content": "Original",
            "description": "**Body**",
            "checked": false,
            "labels": ["invented"],
            "due": {
              "date": "2026-10-08T18:00:00",
              "timezone": "Europe/Amsterdam",
              "is_recurring": true,
              "string": "every Thursday"
            }
          },
          "target": {
            "https://atomicdata.dev/properties/name": "Original",
            "https://atomicdata.dev/task/v1/body": "**Body**",
            "https://atomicdata.dev/task/v1/status": [
              "https://atomicdata.dev/task/v1/todo"
            ],
            "https://atomicdata.dev/task/v1/due-date": "2026-10-08"
          },
          "edits": [
            {
              "target": {
                "https://atomicdata.dev/properties/name": "Edited",
                "https://atomicdata.dev/task/v1/body": "",
                "https://atomicdata.dev/task/v1/status": [
                  "https://atomicdata.dev/task/v1/todo"
                ],
                "https://atomicdata.dev/task/v1/due-date": "2026-10-08"
              },
              "source": {
                "id": "task-a",
                "content": "Edited",
                "description": "",
                "checked": false,
                "labels": ["invented"],
                "due": {
                  "date": "2026-10-08T18:00:00",
                  "timezone": "Europe/Amsterdam",
                  "is_recurring": true,
                  "string": "every Thursday"
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "target": {
                "https://atomicdata.dev/task/v1/status": [
                  "https://atomicdata.dev/task/v1/done"
                ]
              },
              "error": "read-only"
            },
            {
              "target": {
                "https://atomicdata.dev/task/v1/due-date": "2026-10-09"
              },
              "error": "read-only"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "source": {
            "id": "task-b",
            "content": "Done already",
            "description": "",
            "checked": true,
            "due": null
          },
          "target": {
            "https://atomicdata.dev/properties/name": "Done already",
            "https://atomicdata.dev/task/v1/body": "",
            "https://atomicdata.dev/task/v1/status": [
              "https://atomicdata.dev/task/v1/done"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    "raindrop-bookmark-v1": {
      "name": "Raindrop bookmark ↔ Bookmark",
      "description": "A Raindrop.io bookmark record and the host's built-in Bookmark class: title, link and excerpt.",
      "source": {
        "record": { "provider": "raindrop.io", "resource": "raindrop" }
      },
      "target": { "class": "https://atomicdata.dev/class/Bookmark" },
      "mapping": {
        "version": 2,
        "fields": [
          {
            "source": "/title",
            "target": "https://atomicdata.dev/properties/name"
          },
          {
            "source": "/link",
            "target": "https://atomicdata.dev/property/url"
          },
          {
            "source": "/excerpt",
            "target": "https://atomicdata.dev/properties/description"
          }
        ]
      },
      "limits": [
        "No overlay declares a Raindrop crudResource yet, so no catalog integration produces this source; the record endpoint names the shape the code lens reads.",
        "No domain guard: the code lens refuses a non-positive id, titles over 1000 and excerpts over 10000 UTF-16 code units, and a link that is not an absolute http(s) URL.",
        "A row without a description leaves the excerpt unchanged; the code lens writes an empty excerpt. Removal is not expressible."
      ],
      "implementation": "integrations/bookmarks/devonian/raindrop/lens/index.ts",
      "examples": [
        {
          "source": {
            "_id": 41,
            "title": "A bookmark",
            "link": "https://example.org/article",
            "tags": ["invented"],
            "note": "Provider-only note",
            "created": "2026-10-01T12:00:00+02:00"
          },
          "target": {
            "https://atomicdata.dev/properties/name": "A bookmark",
            "https://atomicdata.dev/property/url": "https://example.org/article"
          },
          "edits": [
            {
              "target": {
                "https://atomicdata.dev/properties/name": "Changed",
                "https://atomicdata.dev/property/url": "https://example.org/article",
                "https://atomicdata.dev/properties/description": "Edited"
              },
              "source": {
                "_id": 41,
                "title": "Changed",
                "link": "https://example.org/article",
                "tags": ["invented"],
                "note": "Provider-only note",
                "created": "2026-10-01T12:00:00+02:00",
                "excerpt": "Edited"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "solid-bookmark-v1": {
      "name": "Solid bookmark ↔ Bookmark",
      "description": "An RDF bookmark node in expanded JSON-LD (a Solid Pod document) and the host's built-in Bookmark class: its dcterms:title literal and its bookmark:recalls link.",
      "source": { "rdf": "http://www.w3.org/2002/01/bookmark#Bookmark" },
      "target": { "class": "https://atomicdata.dev/class/Bookmark" },
      "mapping": {
        "version": 2,
        "fields": [
          {
            "source": "/http:~1~1purl.org~1dc~1terms~1title/0/@value",
            "target": "https://atomicdata.dev/properties/name"
          },
          {
            "source": "/http:~1~1www.w3.org~12002~101~1bookmark#recalls/0/@id",
            "target": "https://atomicdata.dev/property/url"
          }
        ]
      },
      "limits": [
        "Only the dcterms:title and bookmark:recalls predicates: the code lens also reads rdfs:label and as:name titles, as:url links, links written as literals, and the bookmark#BookMark and as:Note types, and refuses a node with two title or two link predicates.",
        "No domain guard on the RDF objects: the code lens refuses literals with other datatypes, several objects for one predicate and links that are not absolute http(s) URLs.",
        "The result is a changed node, not a Pod write: a host still needs the document's ETag and, where present, its CRDT protocol."
      ],
      "implementation": "integrations/solid/devonian/bookmarks/lens/index.ts",
      "examples": [
        {
          "source": {
            "@id": "https://pod.example/bookmarks/index.ttl#one",
            "@type": ["http://www.w3.org/2002/01/bookmark#Bookmark"],
            "http://purl.org/dc/terms/title": [
              { "@value": "Original", "@language": "nl" }
            ],
            "http://www.w3.org/2002/01/bookmark#recalls": [
              { "@id": "https://example.org/article" }
            ],
            "http://www.w3.org/2002/01/bookmark#hasTopic": [
              { "@value": "Invented topic" }
            ]
          },
          "target": {
            "https://atomicdata.dev/properties/name": "Original",
            "https://atomicdata.dev/property/url": "https://example.org/article"
          },
          "edits": [
            {
              "target": {
                "https://atomicdata.dev/properties/name": "Changed",
                "https://atomicdata.dev/property/url": "https://example.org/next"
              },
              "source": {
                "@id": "https://pod.example/bookmarks/index.ttl#one",
                "@type": ["http://www.w3.org/2002/01/bookmark#Bookmark"],
                "http://purl.org/dc/terms/title": [
                  { "@value": "Changed", "@language": "nl" }
                ],
                "http://www.w3.org/2002/01/bookmark#recalls": [
                  { "@id": "https://example.org/next" }
                ],
                "http://www.w3.org/2002/01/bookmark#hasTopic": [
                  { "@value": "Invented topic" }
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
